<h1>2. High-throughput ES-A series</h1>
<h2>   Introduction:</h2>
<p>Series cardboard is characterized by its low relative density, high porosity, small thickness, and large absorption capacity, which is especially suitable for rapid clarification applications. It can be used as the initial filtration process for liquids and is widely used to filter viscous liquids, haze liquids containing high concentrations of protein, and liquids containing more solid particles.</p>
<h2>  Advantages and characteristics:</h2>
<ol>
<li>Low density, large gap, it is not easy to block the cardboard when filtering viscous liquid;</li>
<li>The cardboard has a large dirt holding capacity and a large filtering capacity, which can quickly clarify the filtrate;</li>
<li>The porous structure can effectively adsorb suspended solids and effectively reduce the subsequent precipitation;</li>
<li>The product is composed of plant fibers, and the dissolution of metal ions is extremely low.</li>
</ol>
